WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:09.710
Netflix Anime Mega-Rich Two-Hour Special!

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:18.110
Good evening, everyone! Thank you for tuning in.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:23.580
I’m today’s MC, Tenshin Mukai.
Thank you!

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.280
Today we’re presenting a “mega-rich” number of Netflix anime titles!

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.210
That includes hot current titles and brand new ones.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:41.150
We’re streaming on the Netflix Anime Twitter and YouTube accounts.
And we’ll be archived for everyone to enjoy!

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:53.110
Let’s introduce our guests, representing all these great Netflix Anime titles!

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:59.180
Hello, I’m Haruka Shiraishi.
I play Yuri in High-Rise Invasion.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.180
I’m so happy to be here!
And nervous! Thank you!

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.880
Next, Kaji-san.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.610
Hi, I’m Yuki Kaji.
I play Koku in B: The Beginning Succession.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:17.810
Finally season 2 is here for you all to enjoy.
Let’s have fun today!

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.410
Next, Tsuda-san.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:28.350
Hi, I’m Kenjiro Tsuda.
I play Tatsu in The Way of the Househusband.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.280
-I’m nervous!
-No way!

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.710
Next, Kohno-san.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:40.050
Hi, I’m Marika Kohno. I play Sara in Eden.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.410
-I’m nervous too!
-Everyone's saying that!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.380
Next, Shimazaki-san.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.880
Hi, I’m Nobunaga Shimazaki.
I play Baki Hanma in BAKI.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.310
You seem a bit nervous.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:03:05.250
The title and the character are the same.
There’s no mixing it up!

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.710
Last but not least, Kobayashi-san.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:15.910
Hi, I’m Chiaki Kobayashi. I play Yu Ominae,
a member of Spriggan in Spriggan.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:25.780
Thank you all for today.
We’ll be hearing a lot more about your titles over the next two hours.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:34.350
We’ve got a lot of distance here on stage.
I can barely see Kobayashi-san.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:44.510
Let’s still try to enjoy the space.
Tsuda-san, you aren’t really nervous, right?

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:50.050
-I am! I am!
-Your posture is so relaxed!

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.710
My heart is beating.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.850
A great lineup here on stage today.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:05.410
You’ve all been in multiple titles, but is anyone meeting for the first time?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.580
Yes, it’s my first time to meet a lot of you!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:17.510
Me too. Some I’ve met, but haven’t worked together before.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:24.280
Well, we’ll all become friends today, especially at the end.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:32.650
Lots of people I’ve only seen on TV. I kind of feel like a fan!

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:38.850
Let’s get to know each other while introducing these series.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.080
Kaji-san, hello to you too.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:54.380
Such an amazing set, but with lots of social distance.
We’ll have to raise our voices!

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:59.310
Right, there’s a lot of plastic walls to overcome!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.980
Let’s really go for it, everyone!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:13.810
Such volume!
Let’s do it with that passion the whole way through.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:25.180
Please stick with us until the end.
Here’s our first title.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.710
Streaming worldwide,
it’s High-Rise Invasion, starring Shiraishi-san.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.150
First, let’s take a look at this clip!

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.420
I will kill the Mask!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.050
Big brother,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.720
help me!

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.260
I'm on the roof of a building.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.310
There's a strange man with a mask on.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.430
The Mask is there?

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.980
I won't die without seeing my big brother!

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.190
That's the rule of this world. Accept it.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:01.990
The Mask's aim is to drive people
to suicide from despair.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.780
Is there really a human being
inside the Mask?

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.490
May I speak to you?

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.120
This realm is an institution
that creates Gods.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.250
What on earth?
What is "Become a God"?

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.880
My name is Kazuma Aohara.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.800
Could I say that
I am God Candidate within this realm?

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.010
I cannot defy the Mask's orders.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:29.600
Do you know how to access
the Railgun System?

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.020
I want to bring true peace to the world.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:37.270
If you behave disrespectfully,
you will have to die.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.730
I dare you to do it, you fiend!

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.480
I want to die with you!

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:42.940
Mayuko!

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.160
You better not direct
your hostility at me.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.280
I'll become God.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.450
I am right about everything!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.790
Anything that they desire.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.750
I will wipe them out, no matter what!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.290
I am going to die.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.040
Die?

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.040
I will not die!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:21.150
Wow, quite a thrilling clip.
My palms are sweating.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:27.480
“Don’t think, despair.
Screw the rules, break them instead!”

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:32.010
-A pretty impressive slogan!
-Quite strong!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:44.380
A series about a gruesome game of death
from Ajin’s Tsuina Miura and Box!’s Takahiro Oba.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.880
Not just a game of death! A gruesome one!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:57.810
Shiraishi-san, tell us a bit about the show and your character, Yuri Honjo.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:03.780
Like you said, there’s despair from the beginning.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:09.780
The characters can’t come down from
the high rises, and different Masks attack them.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:15.580
How can the characters survive their brutal circumstances?

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:23.450
Yuri loves her brother, and really wants to see him again.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:31.180
But there are so many different Masks! Some perverted ones, even!

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:43.680
Some Masks maintain what they were good at when they were human.
Swimming, baseball, etc.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:58.650
So they attack in various ways. That’s part of the fun.
How will the characters survive? Who can they trust?

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:02.510
Please check it out.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:09.650
Right, the Masks all attack in different ways.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:25.510
Yuri figures out ways to battle them every time.
That’s part of what makes her great.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.310
How about her friend Nise?

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:43.780
It seems like she really likes Yuri.
They have such a nice relationship.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:55.250
It’s a serious show, but with some surreal humor.
That’s fun too.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.350
Thank you!

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:04.610
Next, some key phrases based on a pre-interview with Shiraishi-san.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:15.880
Do any of these phrases pique your interest, Kaji-san?

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:26.450
They’re all interesting, but…
What about the scariest Mask?

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:31.280
There were a lot in the trailer.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:38.950
How about it, Shiraishi-san?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.850
Here it comes.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:46.650
-Is it us?
-No, here it is.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:57.850
The first mask Yuri encounters, right when she wakes up.

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.380
-So scary!
-Right?

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:14.750
The scene is so powerful.
When I read the manga I thought it was so scary.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:25.150
And anime makes it even more real.
In a good way, it’s so scary and thrilling.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:29.480
-It would be terrible to meet that Mask!
-Right?!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:33.580
-He’s the first enemy?
-Yes!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:49.910
-Wielding a Japanese sword! So scary!
-And there are many more!

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:58.050
Let’s ask more! Kaji-san, go ahead.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:14.750
It sounds like a very scary world,
but any scenes you empathize with?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:21.910
Especially in terms of Yuri?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:32.780
It’s quite a scary world.
I asked myself what I would do if I were there.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:51.710
I’m not as strong as Yuri, but she has
a strong goal to see her brother and escape.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:13:12.250
I also move toward goals with a sense of purpose.
I could really sympathize with that.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:19.510
Keeping her cool in serious situations.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:23.310
It’s not just serious, though.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:34.680
Nise-chan is a bit of a tsundere.
But she opens herself up to Yuri.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:52.150
She wants to hug but worries about not having showered, etc.
She’s so cute.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:14:05.280
Even among serious scenes there’s comical parts.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:18.450
Speaking of High-Rise Invasion, we asked the whole group one more question.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:24.110
“Which guest here today is closest to God status?”

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:32.350
Probably the first and last time you’ll ever be asked that!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:35.450
Let’s see the results!

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:45.310
Wow, four people picked Tsuda-san.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.650
Shirashi-san, why Tsuda-san?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:15:03.110
I’d known about Tsuda-san for a long time, and it was exciting to work with him.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:14.750
When he’s acting in front of me, it’s so thrilling.
He’s like a god of acting.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:21.010
-A god of acting!
-Thank you!

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:26.910
Three more people! Kaji-san?

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:40.410
Just look at him, he’s a god!
If I were a god, I’m ask him to make me a voice actor!

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.250
Two gods, huh?

00:15:44.250 --> 00:16:04.510
He’s so good at acting, he’s a god.
And he gives such specific advice.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:18.910
We once ate together and he gave me
some advice on something I was worried about.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:29.880
-I’m still thankful to him.
-Anytime!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.950
Shimazaki-san?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:43.210
His sex appeal.
Even as a fellow guy, he’s so sexy. And humorous.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:50.810
-A sexy god.
-Yeah, so cool.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:53.210
Kobayashi-san?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:17:18.110
He ticks all the boxes for my ideal guy image.
Like his beard, and of course his voice.

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:22.610
Tsuda-san, you’re being praised a lot here.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:31.280
-Well, I'm closest to heaven in terms of age.
-No, no, not that!

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:41.110
We’ll be asking questions like this for all the shows.
Stay tuned.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:55.280
The answers we didn’t have time
for will be uploaded to Netflix’s social media!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:18:00.250
High-Rise Invasion is now streaming worldwide!
Please check it out!

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:04.410
Next up is...

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:16.650
B: The Beginning Succession, starring Kaji-san.
It just started streaming last month.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.580
First, let’s check out this trailer!

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.420
Koku, we need
your blade and your power.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.710
You survived?

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.840
Then what about all the others?

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.970
So let's do this together.

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.220
If you don't accept my offer,

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.430
they'll all die.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:36.560
Wiped out&nbsp;
like they were never here.

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:45.230
After all my searching,
I found you, Koku.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:47.230
No. Killer B.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.030
Citizens have already begun

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:56.700
to voice their fears&nbsp;
about the dangers

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.450
of serial murders starting up again.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:18:59.450
Mother of God!

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.750
Lily, go find Keith.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:02.920
Yeah, I'm on it.

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.760
So this was a trap.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.760
Keith has been kidnapped.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.060
Then it's vengeance.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:29.400
Those who kill God
will become devils,

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.030
whereas devil killers
become kings.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.280
Be careful, everyone!

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:54.380
There are still a great many things
that you remain ignorant to.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:10.980
Every scene is so cool
I’ve got goosebumps.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:20.310
It’s directed by Kazuto Nakazawa,
who worked on titles like Kill Bill. It’s animated at Production I.G.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:26.450
B: The Beginning has won worldwide acclaim.
It was even featured at the 42nd Annecy Animation Film Festival!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:31.280
Now the second season is finally here!
The theme song is performed by ACCAMER!

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:36.710
Kaji-san, what can you tell us about the show and your character, Koku?

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:46.680
It’s a complicated story, so I’m not sure where to start.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:53.850
Succession is season 2 of the show.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:21:01.810
Season 1 ended with the possibility of a continuation.

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:16.150
Keith on the police side, played by Hiroaki Hirata, and me as Koku on the other side.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:20.050
A good balance.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:33.550
A key word in the show is “B,” with a unique logo.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:46.710
It appears at the murder scenes each time, along with a four-fingered slash.
It’s the mark of Killer B.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:54.010
Season 1 was about who Killer B was.

00:21:54.010 --> 00:22:00.280
It was actually Koku, who I play.

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:25.710
“B” meant “13,” and the “4” flash represented Yuna, who he searched for.

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:38.550
It’s like a psycho-suspense with battle fantasy.
It tries a lot of new things in the world of anime.

00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:45.680
Battles, mysteries… it’s a great show.

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:53.880
Next, some key phrases based on a pre-interview with Kaji-san.

00:22:55.480 --> 00:23:01.750
Tsuda-san, do any of these words pique your interest?

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:11.550
So many amazing scenes, but how about your favorite scene?

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:17.950
There are lots of scenes, but what’s your favorite?

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:26.580
Well, there are lots.. battles, great animation.

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:34.710
But my favorite are those with Keith, played by Hirata-san.

00:23:34.710 --> 00:23:41.380
It’s like watching a TV series from abroad.
His voice and acting are so good.

00:23:41.380 --> 00:24:01.010
It’s anime but it feels like reality.
Sometimes Hirata-san’s lines are 2-3 pages at a time!

00:24:01.010 --> 00:24:13.480
Keith is called Genie, or “genius,” in the show.
I really love his long lines.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:31.110
But when Hirata-san looks at those long lines,
he says “can I take a break next week?”

00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:37.910
“I’ll give half the lines to you.”

00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:52.550
He’s a charming guy, not just cool.
Hirata-san really brings out the charm of that character.

00:24:54.450 --> 00:24:59.750
That adds even more charm to the show!

00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:05.980
One more, Tsuda-san?

00:25:05.980 --> 00:25:16.710
-Which character would be a great partner?
-Out of all the RIS characters?

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:35.250
There’s a character called Kaela.
She’s at HQ, as a navigator.

00:25:35.250 --> 00:25:47.710
There are lots of computers in front of her,
and she even uses her feet to operate them!

00:25:47.710 --> 00:25:49.580
Wow, like an instrument?

00:25:49.580 --> 00:26:00.550
It’s so cool, I would love to have her as support.

00:26:00.550 --> 00:26:12.010
You could succeed even if you weren’t that good yourself.

00:26:12.010 --> 00:26:15.550
She might be the best partner.

00:26:15.550 --> 00:26:20.780
Wow, using her feet, it’s like playing drums!

00:26:21.150 --> 00:26:27.080
There are lots of unique characters.
Please give it a watch.

00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:38.350
Speaking of B: The Beginning Succession, we asked the group one more question.

00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:43.910
"Which guest might have an unexpected side?"

00:26:43.910 --> 00:26:46.510
Let’s see the answers.

00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:57.350
Two people chose Shiraishi-san.
Let’s ask about her.

00:26:57.350 --> 00:27:01.680
Tsuda-san?

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:15.580
She’s always smiling. I’ve never seen her angry.
I bet she’d be really scary when angry.

00:27:15.580 --> 00:27:23.380
-This isn’t really praise, is it?
-But you did say she’s nice.

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:26.450
Do you get angry?

00:27:26.450 --> 00:27:32.210
I’m not sure how I’d be if I really got mad.

00:27:32.210 --> 00:27:44.350
It might happen sometime?
Yikes, don’t get her angry!

00:27:44.350 --> 00:27:49.250
Kobayashi-san, how about you?

00:27:49.250 --> 00:28:03.110
We haven't really met, this is just my impression.
But when I searched online she was smiling a lot.

00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:14.310
She seems like she has enough courage to even smash bugs while smiling!

00:28:14.310 --> 00:28:25.380
Even to catch cockroaches with a smile!

00:28:25.380 --> 00:28:32.250
-Can you do that?
-No way!

00:28:32.250 --> 00:28:39.210
-Oh, she got a bit angry just now!
-She might come for me!

00:28:39.210 --> 00:28:49.950
-Shiraishi-san, you chose Tsuda-san?
-Yes, I chose him again.

00:28:49.950 --> 00:29:00.110
He plays cool characters, but when we met he was so nice.

00:29:00.110 --> 00:29:10.280
He really cheers you on. That’s different from his persona.

00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:17.010
-I’m getting praised again!
-It’s becoming a theme!

00:29:17.010 --> 00:29:26.110
He likes tapioca milk tea, too.
He’s a bit cute. Not just cool.

00:29:26.110 --> 00:29:37.180
Why all this praise?
Today’s a Tsuda-san praise fest!

00:29:37.180 --> 00:29:44.350
It’s interesting to think about these persona gaps!
Might give our viewers food for thought.

00:29:44.350 --> 00:29:55.880
B: The Beginning Succession is now streaming worldwide!
Check it out along with season 1!

00:29:55.880 --> 00:30:00.510
Okay, let’s move onto the next title.

00:30:05.710 --> 00:30:11.650
Starring Tsuda-san and coming to Netflix
April 8 worldwide, it’s The Way of the Househusband!

00:30:11.650 --> 00:30:14.650
First, let’s check out the trailer!

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:17.770
Once,

00:30:17.860 --> 00:30:20.480
there was a legendary yakuza,

00:30:20.570 --> 00:30:22.240
feared in the world
of organized crime.

00:30:23.030 --> 00:30:24.610
The Immortal Dragon.

00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:27.030
However, one day,

00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:31.080
the man vanished without a trace
and is now…

00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:32.790
Occupation?

00:30:33.500 --> 00:30:35.250
Full-time househusband.

00:30:40.460 --> 00:30:41.880
For the family I love,

00:30:42.880 --> 00:30:45.300
I will weather
the Way of the Househusband!

00:30:45.380 --> 00:30:49.010
This is uncut, 100% hand-sewn.

00:30:49.100 --> 00:30:50.100
Come on, just buy it!

00:30:50.470 --> 00:30:52.890
I won't buy you games
if you act like a spoiled brat!

00:30:54.890 --> 00:30:56.400
Hamburger meal.

00:30:56.480 --> 00:30:58.980
Don't you know
light and dark laundry doesn't mix!

00:30:59.060 --> 00:31:00.940
Don't mess with color transfer!

00:31:01.690 --> 00:31:04.320
Why aren't you
attacking the corner?

00:31:04.400 --> 00:31:05.320
Boss!

00:31:05.400 --> 00:31:06.610
Huh?

00:31:07.740 --> 00:31:09.120
Why'd you quit being a yakuza?

00:31:13.700 --> 00:31:14.870
Hey!

00:31:14.960 --> 00:31:17.960
I'm going to protect my own
in my own way.

00:31:18.960 --> 00:31:21.590
You forgot your lunch!

00:31:21.670 --> 00:31:24.210
Daily chores
just became a little more fun

00:31:24.300 --> 00:31:26.130
in this cozy comedy

00:31:26.220 --> 00:31:28.470
exclusively available on NETFLIX.

00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:33.640
NETFLIX is seriously
raking in the dough.

00:31:36.640 --> 00:31:38.100
The Way of the Househusband.

00:31:38.600 --> 00:31:41.820
I'll pay whatever it takes.
Just prepare the goods.

00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:43.980
Also, could you make
a point card for me?

00:31:48.480 --> 00:31:53.780
It looks so funny!
Even from the trailer!

00:31:53.780 --> 00:32:02.410
The hit manga by Kosuke Oono with over 3.6 million
copies in print is now an anime series!

00:32:02.410 --> 00:32:08.580
Legendary former yakuza member Tatsu
is now a househusband in this domestic comedy!

00:32:08.580 --> 00:32:14.780
Tsuda-san joined our AnimeJapan special last week.
It looked like a lot of fun!

00:32:14.780 --> 00:32:19.950
Tsuda-san, what can you tell us about the show and your character, Tatsu?

00:32:21.050 --> 00:32:32.380
Well, just as you saw,
he’s a legendary former yakuza who becomes a househusband.

00:32:32.380 --> 00:32:39.450
He runs into all the usual problems with household chores.

00:32:39.450 --> 00:32:51.180
It’s a domestic gag anime. It’s quite funny.

00:32:51.180 --> 00:32:58.080
Even the pictures here are so funny.

00:32:58.080 --> 00:33:08.880
You can really enjoy it casually.

00:33:10.250 --> 00:33:15.680
It’s got a great cast lineup.
How was the recording?

00:33:15.680 --> 00:33:27.910
Because of the pandemic, we all record separately.
Lots of studios on the same floor.

00:33:27.910 --> 00:33:47.850
I do a few episodes on the same day. 
Just me in a big booth for three.

00:33:47.850 --> 00:33:56.010
A bit lonesome, but the show is interesting so I laugh a lot.

00:33:56.010 --> 00:34:09.650
I could just keep going. So fun.

00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:21.350
Next, some key phrases based on a pre-interview with Tsuda-san.

00:34:21.350 --> 00:34:28.250
Kohno-san, do any of these words pique your interest?

00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:36.980
“Pulling potatoes!”
You don’t hear this much in everyday conversation.

00:34:36.980 --> 00:34:41.850
It must be a yazuka phrase?
I just had to look it up!

00:34:41.850 --> 00:34:56.880
When you pull up a potato, your body language looks as if you’re scared!

00:34:56.880 --> 00:35:00.410
Right!

00:35:00.410 --> 00:35:05.950
Tsuda-san, any “pulling potato” moments?

00:35:05.950 --> 00:35:14.780
Quite a phrase, right?
“Getting scared” or “freaking out.”

00:35:14.780 --> 00:35:23.310
For example, I sometimes go to the wrong studio.

00:35:23.310 --> 00:35:35.280
I go where I think the recording is and get there early.
Have a coffee, take it easy.

00:35:35.280 --> 00:35:41.680
I go in five minutes beforehand.
But then it’s the wrong place!

00:35:41.680 --> 00:35:43.910
-What?
-Never happens to you guys?!

00:35:43.910 --> 00:35:45.810
-It does.
-Right?!

00:35:45.810 --> 00:35:54.050
Not all the time, of course. Sometimes.

00:35:54.050 --> 00:36:10.710
I did it 3 times the other day!
I went to all the wrong rooms in the same studio!

00:36:10.710 --> 00:36:26.810
Wrong, wrong, wrong.
Then finally made it to the right place.

00:36:26.810 --> 00:36:34.910
-You do get scared when you get it wrong.
-A "pulling potato" moment.

00:36:34.910 --> 00:36:39.680
Kohno-san, anything else?

00:36:42.250 --> 00:36:58.310
I think Tsuda-san is so friendly,
so I wonder if he has anything in common with Tatsu?

00:36:58.310 --> 00:37:04.310
Well, not really.
His voice, I guess.

00:37:04.310 --> 00:37:09.080
-Of course!
-It’s you!

00:37:11.080 --> 00:37:21.250
Well, when I meet younger people for the first time, they don’t talk to me.

00:37:21.250 --> 00:37:26.480
Tatsu and I might look hard to talk to.

00:37:26.480 --> 00:37:41.950
You do look scary. You aren’t, though.
You have that god-like aura. Hard to approach.

00:37:41.950 --> 00:37:46.850
-Let's grab a bite soon.
-Oh, thank you!

00:37:46.850 --> 00:37:59.180
-That might be one thing in common.
-Right. Please talk to me, everyone.

00:38:02.110 --> 00:38:07.310
Speaking of The Way of the Househusband, we asked the whole group one more question.

00:38:07.310 --> 00:38:11.710
“Which guest seems best at household chores?”

00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:13.450
Let’s see the answers.

00:38:13.450 --> 00:38:19.010
Two people answered Kobayashi-san.

00:38:19.010 --> 00:38:21.610
Tsuda-san?

00:38:21.610 --> 00:38:31.250
-It seems like you can do anything.
-Based on what?

00:38:31.250 --> 00:38:34.010
-Your atmosphere.
-Atmosphere!

00:38:34.010 --> 00:38:41.050
-You look like a chores (kaji) advisor!
-Do I?

00:38:41.050 --> 00:38:45.450
-An advisor for Kaji-san?
-Kaji-kun, you chose yourself?

00:38:45.450 --> 00:38:51.050
Right, I chose myself because “kaji” means chores!
No deep meaning!

00:38:51.050 --> 00:38:56.150
I thought someone might make that joke.

00:38:56.150 --> 00:39:01.250
I felt like I had to!

00:39:01.250 --> 00:39:07.050
Koyabashi-kun, why do you look so Kaji-like?
Even though you’re not Kaji!

00:39:07.050 --> 00:39:10.610
-Sorry!
-No need to apologize!

00:39:10.610 --> 00:39:15.910
I should look less like I can do chores!

00:39:17.050 --> 00:39:20.010
Kohno-san, why Kobayashi-san?

00:39:20.010 --> 00:39:26.480
-Just based on his face.
-Is my face that Kaji-like?!

00:39:26.480 --> 00:39:30.750
We’ve never met, so I looked him up.

00:39:30.750 --> 00:39:38.410
The first picture looked like a guy who knows chores!

00:39:38.410 --> 00:39:41.750
Thank you!

00:39:41.750 --> 00:39:49.410
-How about in reality?
-I like cleaning.

00:39:49.410 --> 00:39:55.150
But I can’t cook.
I can’t even make rice.

00:39:55.510 --> 00:39:57.650
I've never bought a rice cooker.

00:39:57.650 --> 00:39:59.710
You have a house, right?!

00:39:59.710 --> 00:40:02.950
Yes, with electricity and everything.

00:40:02.950 --> 00:40:09.250
But rice cookers are hard to use.

00:40:09.250 --> 00:40:10.780
Don’t you just press the button?

00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:21.110
-I’ve tried it many times, but it was soaked.
-Too much water!

00:40:21.110 --> 00:40:25.980
-Just use trial and error!
-Nah, it’s quite hard.

00:40:25.980 --> 00:40:30.350
This is the guy picked as “best at chores”!

00:40:30.350 --> 00:40:36.310
Kobayashi-san, please do try your hand at rice cooking.

00:40:36.310 --> 00:40:39.150
I’ll try to live up to my chores face.

00:40:40.350 --> 00:40:52.080
The Way of the Househusband starts streaming worldwide April 8!
Check it out!

00:40:52.080 --> 00:40:57.080
And here’s our next title!

00:41:01.710 --> 00:41:07.750
Coming May 27 and starring Kohno-san, it’s Eden!

00:41:07.750 --> 00:41:10.310
Let’s take a look at this trailer!

00:41:13.130 --> 00:41:14.840
Human language.

00:41:15.710 --> 00:41:17.510
There is a human in this world.

00:41:18.680 --> 00:41:20.410
What would you like to do?

00:41:21.480 --> 00:41:23.210
Eliminate them.

00:41:24.680 --> 00:41:27.380
No one must know
there is a human here.

00:41:28.240 --> 00:41:31.040
Humans are considered to be bad.

00:41:31.110 --> 00:41:32.180
Sara!

00:41:34.110 --> 00:41:36.480
Did the recon squad find out
about this place?

00:41:37.910 --> 00:41:39.310
What are you going to do?

00:41:40.910 --> 00:41:41.810
Stop Zero!

00:41:43.040 --> 00:41:45.610
Zero, are you fully recharged?

00:41:47.740 --> 00:41:50.410
Humans will destroy the world.

00:41:51.010 --> 00:41:52.210
They are evil.

00:41:55.480 --> 00:41:57.080
Humans are not harmful!

00:41:58.740 --> 00:42:00.880
Sara is a very good human.

00:42:02.010 --> 00:42:02.840
Stop!

00:42:03.980 --> 00:42:07.340
Why do you hate humans
so much?

00:42:08.740 --> 00:42:11.480
To create a perfect world,

00:42:12.610 --> 00:42:14.840
humans are a hindrance.

00:42:14.910 --> 00:42:16.240
It can't be…

00:42:22.610 --> 00:42:34.250
Wow, what a trailer.
It was unveiled at AnimeJapan, with Kohno-san in attendance.

00:42:34.250 --> 00:42:38.410
It really leaves you guessing!

00:42:38.410 --> 00:42:45.780
Yes, it’s an original anime, so no one knows what’s coming!

00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:59.850
As you heard in the trailer, “humans are evil.”
There’s a battle between robots and Sara, a human.

00:42:59.850 --> 00:43:05.350
-She goes on a journey for the truth.
-Looks fascinating.

00:43:05.350 --> 00:43:15.410
Eden is directed by Yasuhiro Irie (Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood),
and features the work of top creators worldwide!

00:43:15.410 --> 00:43:17.450
It’s a heartwarming sci-fi fantasy.

00:43:17.450 --> 00:43:23.080
Kohno-san, what can you tell us about the show and your character, Sara?

00:43:23.080 --> 00:43:32.050
My character, Sara, was raised by two robots.

00:43:32.050 --> 00:43:41.850
They can’t speak at first. They’re farmer robots who pick apples.

00:43:41.850 --> 00:43:50.910
Sara was raised by those robots. In this world, there are only robots.

00:43:50.910 --> 00:44:08.150
Why is Sara the only human, where did the rest go?
She goes on an adventure to find out.

00:44:08.150 --> 00:44:14.310
I can’t wait to see it!

00:44:14.310 --> 00:44:20.180
Next, some key phrases based on a pre-interview with Kohno-san.

00:44:20.180 --> 00:44:26.010
Shimazaki-san, do any of these words pique your interest?

00:44:26.010 --> 00:44:32.880
How about working with veteran voice actor Koichi Yamadera?

00:44:32.880 --> 00:44:40.050
How was it?

00:44:40.050 --> 00:44:44.050
He’s like a senpai for all of us.

00:44:44.050 --> 00:44:50.350
We recorded it a while back, in 2017-2018.

00:44:50.350 --> 00:45:05.280
I was new, and didn’t know much about voice recording.
What was acceptable and what wasn’t.

00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:31.480
Zero is played by Yamadera-san.
He’s a robot, but in one scene he drinks then talks.

00:45:31.480 --> 00:45:33.710
It’s a very important scene.

00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:59.410
In the test, Yamadera-san drank his own water then spoke.
I thought, “I see, you can do that!”

00:45:59.410 --> 00:46:08.750
Right in front of the mic.
It was a great learning experience.

00:46:08.750 --> 00:46:14.580
Right, you’re not sure you can do it.

00:46:14.580 --> 00:46:27.550
Of course, it worked because it was Yamadera-san.
If it were me I wouldn’t be sure what to do with the cup!

00:46:27.550 --> 00:46:36.880
I thought he was so cool.

00:46:36.880 --> 00:46:47.210
-What a great learning experience. So nice.
-Indeed.

00:46:47.210 --> 00:46:51.310
Next, Shimazaki-san?

00:46:51.310 --> 00:47:02.280
Hm, how about “warm feeling”?
Or maybe “Eden”?

00:47:02.280 --> 00:47:10.180
Well, I’m not sure how to answer “Eden,” so “warm feeling.”

00:47:10.180 --> 00:47:30.450
-I don’t really do cooking...
-This sounds like a job for Kobayashi-san! Not!

00:47:30.450 --> 00:47:41.250
So, I use a delivery service to order food.
In the app, you can help support restaurants.

00:47:41.250 --> 00:47:53.750
You can add a kind of tip.
I added some extra money.

00:47:53.750 --> 00:48:01.880
Inside my order was a handwritten message thanking me for the support.

00:48:01.880 --> 00:48:12.910
Okay, it sounds a bit silly to be satisfied
just by giving someone some money...

00:48:12.910 --> 00:48:26.650
But it did make me feel happy about helping someone out.

00:48:26.650 --> 00:48:30.250
That would give you a warm feeling.

00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:35.250
Handwritten letters are so nice.

00:48:35.250 --> 00:48:42.910
I get them from fans too, there’s so much love in them.

00:48:42.910 --> 00:48:54.680
Much different from a printed letter.
Those are nice too, of course.

00:48:54.680 --> 00:49:00.310
Speaking of Eden, we’ve asked everyone one more question.

00:49:00.310 --> 00:49:08.980
“Which guest could most easily adapt to another world?”

00:49:08.980 --> 00:49:12.710
Let’s see the answers.

00:49:12.710 --> 00:49:17.480
Three people chose Kaji-san.

00:49:17.480 --> 00:49:23.280
Shiraishi-san, why Kaji-san?

00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:41.280
Based on the characters he plays,
he seems like he could really survive.

00:49:41.280 --> 00:49:43.410
Thank you!

00:49:43.410 --> 00:49:47.080
Until now, it’s basically been Tsuda-san!

00:49:47.080 --> 00:49:54.750
I thought I’d get chosen for the chores (kaji)!

00:49:54.750 --> 00:49:56.410
Shimazaki-san?

00:49:56.410 --> 00:50:04.150
He’s so flexible and adaptable.

00:50:04.150 --> 00:50:22.310
He can do anything, but also thinks of others.
He creates a great environment everywhere.

00:50:22.310 --> 00:50:33.610
-He’s so deliberate.
-Right!

00:50:33.610 --> 00:50:38.850
I understand why Tsuda-san just said he’d buy me a meal…

00:50:38.850 --> 00:50:47.150
-I didn’t say “buy”!
-Oh! Oops! Thank you, everyone.

00:50:47.150 --> 00:50:48.810
Kobayashi-san?

00:50:48.810 --> 00:51:01.750
Kaji-san’s been in so much anime, surrounded by Titans, or by breasts!

00:51:01.750 --> 00:51:09.350
He won’t be so surprised by anything.

00:51:09.350 --> 00:51:19.250
-He has so much experience
-Right.

00:51:19.250 --> 00:51:31.680
Yes, I have been in many genres…
But I chose Tsuda-san for that reason.

00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:43.110
-So much life experience.
-Is that praise?!

00:51:43.110 --> 00:52:01.310
But you can learn from him as a person and as an actor. So cool.

00:52:01.310 --> 00:52:07.450
But it looks like they’re telling us to move on!

00:52:07.450 --> 00:52:18.180
Yes! But there are more questions! Please praise him then!

00:52:18.180 --> 00:52:29.410
Eden hits Netflix worldwide starting May 27!
Check it out!

00:52:29.410 --> 00:52:32.410
Here’s our next title!

00:52:37.150 --> 00:52:39.550
Baki Hanma, starring Shimazaki-san.

00:52:39.550 --> 00:52:41.510
First, let’s check out this teaser!

00:52:42.530 --> 00:52:43.530
Fight me.

00:52:48.860 --> 00:52:50.110
PRACTICAL SHADOW FIGHTING

00:52:53.190 --> 00:52:54.280
PRISON BATTLE

00:52:57.150 --> 00:52:58.360
WILDMAN WAR
THE PICKLE WARS

00:53:01.360 --> 00:53:02.940
STRONGEST FATHER-SON BATTLE IN HISTORY

00:53:03.030 --> 00:53:04.070
THE WORLD IS WAITING

00:53:09.440 --> 00:53:11.280
I'm going to go all out.

00:53:14.010 --> 00:53:20.280
It’s the climax of BAKI.
The strongest father-son battle in history!

00:53:20.280 --> 00:53:25.710
Baki Hanma, smashing onto Netflix worldwide in 2021!

00:53:25.710 --> 00:53:33.550
Finally, Baki Hanma in anime form.

00:53:33.550 --> 00:53:38.350
There are a lot of crazy looking opponents.

00:53:38.350 --> 00:53:42.850
I’m sure fans of the manga are looking forward to seeing it on screen!

00:53:42.850 --> 00:53:47.950
Shimazaki-san, what can you tell us about this season?

00:53:47.950 --> 00:53:58.380
Well, Yujiro Hanma is known as the world’s strongest creature.
Played wonderfully by Akio Otsuka.

00:53:58.380 --> 00:54:06.410
He’s so strong he can create treaties between countries with his might alone.

00:54:06.410 --> 00:54:19.210
Every satellite is tracking him, so GPS itself gets thrown off when he moves!

00:54:19.210 --> 00:54:22.850
-Such power!
-Right?

00:54:22.850 --> 00:54:36.250
That means his son, Baki, has had a tough life!
Oh, here’s some key art drawn by Itagaki-sensei.

00:54:36.250 --> 00:54:41.080
The series tracks Baki’s changes and growth.

00:54:41.080 --> 00:54:53.110
The stories are so wild they seem like lies!
The cast is great too.

00:54:53.110 --> 00:54:59.380
When we did the previous season, Tsuda-san was in it.

00:54:59.380 --> 00:55:06.910
There were five leads, and he was the youngest!

00:55:06.910 --> 00:55:20.750
In other words, the gods above the gods!
So many amazing voices. So husky.

00:55:20.750 --> 00:55:25.580
The show is so fun both visually and aurally.

00:55:25.580 --> 00:55:31.910
Next, some key phrases based on a pre-interview with Shimazaki-san.

00:55:31.910 --> 00:55:43.680
Lots of great keywords…
Here’s something from director Toshiki Hirano.

00:55:43.680 --> 00:55:46.210
Whoa, I didn’t know about this.

00:55:46.210 --> 00:55:55.910
It’s a surprise message from director Hirano.
Let me read it out.

00:55:57.080 --> 00:56:09.150
“You’ve reached the same level as Otsuka-san.
Great work. You’ve surpassed my expectations.”

00:56:09.150 --> 00:56:11.380
He’s really praising you!

00:56:11.380 --> 00:56:14.610
It’s really wild this time!

00:56:14.610 --> 00:56:19.810
The main fight is with Biscuit Oliva, who has so much muscle!

00:56:19.810 --> 00:56:31.110
He’s played by Hochu Otsuka.
He’s not just cool, but charming.

00:56:31.110 --> 00:56:41.350
I have to work hard to even get close to his level!

00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:47.310
The director says you’re on the same level!

00:56:47.310 --> 00:56:49.250
I’m so happy!

00:56:49.250 --> 00:56:58.310
I can’t wait to see this!

00:56:58.310 --> 00:57:01.510
Kobayashi-san, how about these keywords?

00:57:01.510 --> 00:57:10.380
How about “sum it up in one word”?

00:57:10.380 --> 00:57:23.410
Muscles! It’s all about muscles!
Biscuit has so many muscles.

00:57:23.410 --> 00:57:50.980
He says, “there’s hidden muscle within me.”
If I release all my muscles, they’ll bust through the walls and to heaven!

00:57:50.980 --> 00:57:55.910
BAKI’s so crazy!

00:57:55.910 --> 00:58:13.350
But Baki says, “no, no way.”
But Hochu-san is so persuasive. He convinces Baki.

00:58:13.350 --> 00:58:17.510
But that’s how important muscles are this time.

00:58:17.510 --> 00:58:28.610
-I can’t wait!
-It’s definitely exciting!

00:58:28.610 --> 00:58:35.480
Speaking of Baki Hanma, we’ve asked everyone to fill in these blanks.

00:58:35.480 --> 00:58:41.750
“Out of everyone here, (blank) is really strong at (blank).”

00:58:41.750 --> 00:58:44.710
Let’s see the answers!

00:58:44.710 --> 00:58:53.210
Kohno-san and Tsuda-san got two picks each.

00:58:53.210 --> 00:58:58.410
Shiraishi-san, you picked Kohno-san.

00:59:00.280 --> 00:59:03.350
She’s just so cute.

00:59:03.350 --> 00:59:17.510
The first time we met, I was blown away by her cute voice.
Like a twittering bird.

00:59:17.510 --> 00:59:25.510
-And she’s so beautiful.
-No, no!

00:59:25.510 --> 00:59:34.380
-Cuteness is strength!
-Right!

00:59:34.380 --> 00:59:38.250
Everyone’s full of praise today!

00:59:39.450 --> 00:59:44.410
I picked Shiraishi-san for the “god” question.

00:59:44.410 --> 00:59:59.710
I was a minor character on a show she starred in.
During the break, she came and talked to me.

00:59:59.710 --> 01:00:12.750
It’s not so common for minor and main characters to talk.
Main actors are usually so busy.

01:00:12.750 --> 01:00:21.680
But Shiraishi-san came and talked to me. So compassionate!

01:00:21.680 --> 01:00:28.950
-”Compassionate!”
-You don’t hear that much!

01:00:28.950 --> 01:00:33.080
She’s like an angel!

01:00:33.080 --> 01:00:38.680
Tsuda-san, you chose Kohno-san.

01:00:39.610 --> 01:00:44.110
She seems really strong at video games.

01:00:46.150 --> 01:00:49.050
Thank you! I’m so happy!

01:00:49.980 --> 01:01:00.680
There are a lot of voice actors who love games.
I’m so happy Tsuda-san noticed me!

01:01:00.680 --> 01:01:05.610
-How nice!
-Yeah!

01:01:06.610 --> 01:01:12.910
Kaji-san, you chose Tsuda-san, of course!

01:01:12.910 --> 01:01:25.280
I might talk so much we’d have no time for Spriggan!
I mean, I already called him a god!

01:01:25.280 --> 01:01:31.010
-Right, gods are powerful!
-Right!

01:01:31.010 --> 01:01:35.250
-Who else picked Tsuda-san?
-Kohno-san.

01:01:37.680 --> 01:01:46.510
-Tsuda-san is so great.
-Compassionate?

01:01:46.510 --> 01:02:04.880
Yes! I always ask my senpais for advice. Tsuda-san praised me for that.

01:02:04.880 --> 01:02:15.110
She even asked Tessho Genda-san for advice! So great!

01:02:15.110 --> 01:02:22.780
You like to involve everyone!

01:02:22.780 --> 01:02:29.250
Yes, I asked Genda-san for some narration advice.

01:02:29.250 --> 01:02:35.650
Tsuda-san is so good at praise, and watches everyone thoroughly.

01:02:35.650 --> 01:02:38.310
He made me so happy.

01:02:38.310 --> 01:02:47.080
It feels like Tsuda-san is everyone’s god.

01:02:47.080 --> 01:02:48.710
We’ve also got a godly MC!

01:02:48.710 --> 01:02:55.910
No, no! They’re telling me to hurry up!

01:02:55.910 --> 01:03:06.110
Baki Hanma hits Netflix worldwide in 2021!

01:03:06.110 --> 01:03:11.150
Check out the previous seasons streaming now and look forward to it!

01:03:11.340 --> 01:03:14.240
Here is the next show
we're showing you today!

01:03:32.070 --> 01:03:34.850
Here exists a single tablet.

01:03:35.940 --> 01:03:39.200
Beings
of an ancient civilization,

01:03:39.230 --> 01:03:41.070
whose great advances
resulted in their downfall,

01:03:41.770 --> 01:03:44.550
relayed a warning
to the present generation

01:03:44.580 --> 01:03:45.590
through this notice.

01:03:47.160 --> 01:03:48.360
They wrote,

01:03:49.040 --> 01:03:52.160
"Protect our legacy
from evildoers."

01:03:53.450 --> 01:03:55.610
An organization sincerely
accepted this message

01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:59.910
and actively seeks to keep
the ancient civilization sealed.

01:04:00.780 --> 01:04:03.170
And the special agents
of that organization...

01:04:05.090 --> 01:04:06.550
are called "Spriggan."

01:04:25.520 --> 01:04:27.670
There you have it.

01:04:27.930 --> 01:04:31.490
Spriggan finally
gets an anime adaptation.

01:04:31.570 --> 01:04:37.440
Spriggan, started in 1989
in Shogakukan’s Weekly Shonen Sunday,

01:04:37.490 --> 01:04:42.000
and created by Hiroshi Takashige
and Ryoji Minagawa,

01:04:42.080 --> 01:04:47.140
leaps onto the screen 30 years later
with a vivid blend of 2D and 3D animation!

01:04:47.530 --> 01:04:53.370
It’s a high-tempo, battle action series
revolving around ancient ruins!

01:04:53.470 --> 01:04:57.480
Kobayashi-san, I’m sure there’s a lot
you can’t reveal yet.

01:04:58.110 --> 01:05:00.520
If there's anything you can tell us...

01:05:00.640 --> 01:05:05.050
How about your character, Yu Ominae,

01:05:05.130 --> 01:05:08.710
and the series?

01:05:09.200 --> 01:05:13.330
The narration explained a little bit

01:05:13.390 --> 01:05:20.380
but Spriggan is a team
that seals ancient artifacts.

01:05:20.410 --> 01:05:22.680
They're the ARCAM corporation.

01:05:22.770 --> 01:05:27.770
Spriggan are the cream of the crop agents
who protect the artifacts.

01:05:27.930 --> 01:05:34.560
The Spriggan fight bad guys that come after the artifacts

01:05:34.730 --> 01:05:38.680
and bad guys from all different countries.

01:05:38.750 --> 01:05:42.130
It's a sci-fi battle series.

01:05:42.320 --> 01:05:49.830
But are Spriggan and ARCAM Corporation,
trying to seal the artifacts, the good guys?

01:05:50.370 --> 01:05:52.420
Are the enemies really evil?

01:05:52.470 --> 01:05:57.200
The series touches on that
and is really deep.

01:05:57.240 --> 01:05:59.130
I see.

01:05:59.360 --> 01:06:03.410
I'm sure many viewers will
take an interest hearing this.

01:06:03.660 --> 01:06:07.920
The cast was only just announced recently.

01:06:08.120 --> 01:06:12.570
You said recording
sessions have been “throat-crushing”!

01:06:12.680 --> 01:06:16.900
Are the scenes pretty intense?

01:06:16.960 --> 01:06:20.270
I usually look like the upper right face.

01:06:20.360 --> 01:06:24.460
What? Not the face in the middle?

01:06:24.500 --> 01:06:29.420
Yu only looks like that
a few seconds every episode.

01:06:29.460 --> 01:06:31.530
So he's mostly shouting?

01:06:31.600 --> 01:06:36.090
He's shouting or talking with an attitude.

01:06:36.150 --> 01:06:37.200
What?

01:06:37.260 --> 01:06:38.630
That's his character.

01:06:38.720 --> 01:06:41.050
-He does?
-Yes.

01:06:41.210 --> 01:06:45.950
It must be tough
but an awesome role to play?

01:06:46.010 --> 01:06:50.280
Absolutely. We haven't announced
the rest of the cast yet

01:06:50.350 --> 01:06:55.300
but we have many experienced
voice actors on the cast.

01:06:55.360 --> 01:07:01.730
I have much to learn
working together with them.

01:07:01.800 --> 01:07:03.100
It's a wonderful experience.

01:07:03.140 --> 01:07:09.040
I see. We have put together
another board of keywords.

01:07:09.170 --> 01:07:10.630
Let's take a look.

01:07:11.250 --> 01:07:14.620
Shiraishi-san,
please choose from the five keywords.

01:07:14.850 --> 01:07:17.360
-Yes.
-Please choose one.

01:07:17.430 --> 01:07:20.880
This is such a big title.

01:07:20.920 --> 01:07:25.630
As a fellow voice actor,
I'd like to ask about the audition.

01:07:25.680 --> 01:07:28.950
Of course. How was the audition?

01:07:29.050 --> 01:07:34.370
-I auditioned for Yu and another role.
-You did?

01:07:34.420 --> 01:07:40.030
I've never done a role like Yu
who's always shouting.

01:07:40.180 --> 01:07:46.430
I thought if I were going to get a role,
it would be the other role.

01:07:46.660 --> 01:07:50.690
Instead I got Yu, so I was shocked.

01:07:51.490 --> 01:07:53.590
-It happens.
-It does?

01:07:53.650 --> 01:07:56.410
-Right?
-Yeah.

01:07:56.650 --> 01:07:59.600
You get the least expected roles.

01:07:59.670 --> 01:08:06.660
And you don't get the roles you
felt confident auditioning for.

01:08:06.820 --> 01:08:11.400
Maybe you're more relaxed
or less calculated.

01:08:11.470 --> 01:08:15.620
When you're confident,
it's going as you planned.

01:08:15.680 --> 01:08:16.780
-I see.
-Yeah.

01:08:16.840 --> 01:08:19.210
Maybe that's why it's no good.

01:08:19.270 --> 01:08:21.800
It's not that it's no good.

01:08:21.900 --> 01:08:26.150
You got the role.
You did a great job at acting.

01:08:26.190 --> 01:08:29.770
I had fun playing both roles.

01:08:29.810 --> 01:08:32.880
-I see.
-It was just surprising I got Yu.

01:08:33.140 --> 01:08:38.290
Now it will open a new path
for you as an actor.

01:08:38.440 --> 01:08:40.030
It's a wonderful thing.

01:08:40.310 --> 01:08:44.090
Shiraishi-san. Next question, please.

01:08:44.150 --> 01:08:47.230
-Which word?
-Let me see.

01:08:47.530 --> 01:08:52.080
-Memorable characters, please.
-Sure.

01:08:52.140 --> 01:08:56.780
Perhaps this is based on
reading the original manga.

01:08:56.850 --> 01:08:59.440
Are there any memorable characters
besides Yu?

01:08:59.510 --> 01:09:05.820
The enemies in Spriggan
are all full of appeal.

01:09:05.940 --> 01:09:11.000
I especially like Iwao Akatsuki.

01:09:11.060 --> 01:09:14.440
He's a really nice, bulky guy.
Well, most of them are.

01:09:14.510 --> 01:09:17.830
-Of course. Being a special agent.
-Right.

01:09:17.950 --> 01:09:24.050
He is your quintessential enemy
and so cut-throat.

01:09:24.680 --> 01:09:29.070
He just wants to kill Yu.

01:09:29.270 --> 01:09:38.520
But he sometimes shows his nice side and helps Yu out.

01:09:38.860 --> 01:09:45.970
He even has cute banter with the heroine
and shows a sense of humor.

01:09:46.730 --> 01:09:48.720
I love that side of him.

01:09:48.790 --> 01:09:54.040
I also had a chance to record with
the voice actor who plays Akatsuki.

01:09:54.270 --> 01:09:56.990
I can't reveal who the cast is yet.

01:09:57.450 --> 01:10:02.070
But his acting is amazing.

01:10:02.340 --> 01:10:06.920
Due to COVID-19 we recorded alone.

01:10:07.130 --> 01:10:10.370
It ended up being a unique experience for me.

01:10:10.700 --> 01:10:16.850
I got to chat with the person who
plays my enemy during our break.

01:10:16.980 --> 01:10:24.080
We really got to develop
a bond, which is rare.

01:10:24.170 --> 01:10:30.810
It makes Akatsuki
all the more special to me.

01:10:31.040 --> 01:10:35.550
So the character and the actor is special.

01:10:35.600 --> 01:10:41.840
Now we can't wait to find out who the cast is.

01:10:42.050 --> 01:10:47.210
It's time to praise one another yet again.

01:10:48.460 --> 01:10:50.950
Speaking of Spriggan,
we also asked our cast,

01:10:50.980 --> 01:10:56.070
Who among today’s cast do you think has special powers?

01:10:56.450 --> 01:10:58.400
What would that power be?

01:10:58.550 --> 01:11:03.140
Let's take a look at the answers.

01:11:04.200 --> 01:11:06.290
This is strange.

01:11:06.650 --> 01:11:10.070
Shimazaki-san pointed to everyone.

01:11:10.240 --> 01:11:12.800
That's why there are so many lines.

01:11:12.860 --> 01:11:17.400
Let's ask why he pointed to everyone.

01:11:17.560 --> 01:11:20.910
It's our voice acting skills.

01:11:21.710 --> 01:11:26.340
I think it's an amazing skill,
and I don't mean it as a joke.

01:11:26.410 --> 01:11:31.960
I really think
that the skills of voice actors are unique.

01:11:32.040 --> 01:11:39.030
It's something we can be proud of
and we are each recognized actors.

01:11:39.210 --> 01:11:43.340
I think we all have a special skill
in that sense.

01:11:44.960 --> 01:11:49.640
Watching this show makes me feel so happy.

01:11:50.740 --> 01:11:53.160
You all have something nice
to say about each other.

01:11:53.200 --> 01:11:59.310
You're right.
Voice acting skills are a special skill.

01:11:59.930 --> 01:12:03.280
Who else shall I ask?

01:12:03.480 --> 01:12:07.720
-Kaji-san chose Shimazaki-san?
-Yes.

01:12:07.780 --> 01:12:13.360
-I've nothing to add.
-Knock it off!

01:12:13.400 --> 01:12:15.470
You praise one another and that's it?

01:12:16.530 --> 01:12:18.480
What more can I say?

01:12:18.510 --> 01:12:22.190
-On top of that.
-On top?

01:12:23.150 --> 01:12:27.460
I chose Nobunaga-kun.

01:12:27.510 --> 01:12:31.030
He's a little weird.

01:12:31.860 --> 01:12:34.900
-Weird?
-Does that count as a special skill?

01:12:35.040 --> 01:12:40.000
He hasn't outgrown his childishness.

01:12:40.060 --> 01:12:42.270
I probably haven't either.

01:12:42.400 --> 01:12:47.620
He enjoys it and uses it
as his strength in his work.

01:12:47.660 --> 01:12:53.520
It adds to his special skills
as a voice actor, so I chose him.

01:12:54.310 --> 01:12:55.630
I know.

01:12:57.160 --> 01:12:58.930
I'm ready.

01:12:59.050 --> 01:13:00.900
-Nice.
-What skill is that?

01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:03.030
That's a special skill.

01:13:03.090 --> 01:13:07.650
-He didn't need sound effects?
-Incredible.

01:13:07.710 --> 01:13:09.920
But he wasn't Baki.

01:13:10.950 --> 01:13:17.200
You really do have special skills.
Incredible.

01:13:17.380 --> 01:13:22.100
I wanted to ask more but alas!

01:13:22.990 --> 01:13:28.970
We've been on air for over an hour.
How time flies!

01:13:28.990 --> 01:13:31.910
On to the next segment.

01:13:31.930 --> 01:13:36.720
Spriggan will be streamed
worldwide in 2021!

01:13:36.870 --> 01:13:38.270
Let’s look forward to it!

01:13:38.650 --> 01:13:42.230
From here we're going to
change the swing of things.

01:13:42.500 --> 01:13:46.680
We're going to do a games segment.

01:13:47.170 --> 01:13:49.620
No we're not. I made a boo boo.

01:13:50.160 --> 01:13:56.080
I was in such a rush
I almost skipped an entire segment.

01:13:56.220 --> 01:14:01.170
Aside from titles
that our guests tonight are starring in,

01:14:01.200 --> 01:14:04.640
Netflix has a mega-rich lineup of anime
to look forward to.

01:14:04.670 --> 01:14:07.230
We have three titles to preview today.

01:14:07.440 --> 01:14:08.940
First, we have Yasuke.

01:14:09.090 --> 01:14:12.760
Let’s watch this trailer
just released on April 2.

01:15:38.820 --> 01:15:41.130
Set in feudal Japan,

01:15:41.220 --> 01:15:44.470
it is about Yasuke,
the first African to become a samurai.

01:15:44.500 --> 01:15:47.970
He decides to pick up his sword once more

01:15:48.000 --> 01:15:53.060
to protect a girl with mysterious powers
from dark forces.

01:15:53.100 --> 01:15:58.410
Netflix Original Series Yasuke
will stream worldwide

01:15:58.430 --> 01:16:00.970
starting Thursday,
April 29, 2021.

01:16:01.270 --> 01:16:03.980
Next is Record of Ragnarok.

01:16:04.010 --> 01:16:06.560
Please take a look at this clip.

01:16:08.250 --> 01:16:10.160
Thirteen one-on-one matches

01:16:10.440 --> 01:16:13.290
between gods and men
will take place

01:16:13.390 --> 01:16:14.780
Thirteen one-on-one matches

01:16:14.840 --> 01:16:16.150
"Ragnarok."

01:16:17.820 --> 01:16:19.860
You wish not to stand
in the same ring as me?

01:16:20.050 --> 01:16:21.730
Are you perhaps

01:16:22.440 --> 01:16:25.160
scared?

01:16:28.820 --> 01:16:32.650
There is no one in this world
who can rival me

01:16:32.710 --> 01:16:34.140
I have one request.

01:16:34.310 --> 01:16:35.290
Do not die.

01:16:35.330 --> 01:16:39.310
You're a nasty one, aren't you?

01:16:39.710 --> 01:16:42.120
Don't look at me,
you perverted old man.

01:16:44.240 --> 01:16:46.420
For the first time in millennia,
my blood is running hot.

01:16:46.470 --> 01:16:48.320
I'm getting excited.

01:16:48.370 --> 01:16:50.310
File number one.

01:16:50.640 --> 01:16:51.650
It's sour.

01:16:52.190 --> 01:16:55.240
Ganryu is still evolving.

01:16:56.450 --> 01:16:57.560
Sounds like fun.

01:16:57.940 --> 01:17:00.010
I'm so jealous of that human.

01:17:00.840 --> 01:17:02.710
This is a fight for the soul.

01:17:04.060 --> 01:17:05.160
Crush him.

01:17:06.370 --> 01:17:07.380
They're all trash.

01:17:30.570 --> 01:17:35.560
The mega-hit manga finally
gets an anime adaptation!

01:17:35.720 --> 01:17:39.180
The curtain opens on the ultimate showdown
between gods and humans

01:17:39.380 --> 01:17:46.500
whose one-on-one battles will determine
the survival of mankind!!

01:17:46.700 --> 01:17:50.030
Netflix original anime series
Record of Ragnarok

01:17:50.090 --> 01:17:54.670
will stream from June 2021!
What a treat!

01:17:55.210 --> 01:17:58.700
Next is RESIDENT EVIL: Infinite Darkness.

01:17:58.750 --> 01:18:00.440
We have another teaser.

01:18:55.460 --> 01:18:58.110
It is a brand new 3DCG animation

01:18:58.130 --> 01:19:01.780
based on the globally popular
survival horror game Resident Evil.

01:19:01.980 --> 01:19:06.180
It is a horror-action story centered
around the popular characters

01:19:06.320 --> 01:19:09.310
Leon S. Kennedy and Claire Redfield.

01:19:09.550 --> 01:19:15.170
Please enjoy the first CG drama series
on such a titanic scale.

01:19:15.350 --> 01:19:19.620
Netflix original anime series
RESIDENT EVIL: Infinite Darkness

01:19:19.640 --> 01:19:23.760
will stream worldwide in 2021.

01:19:23.950 --> 01:19:26.250
What a lineup!

01:19:26.270 --> 01:19:30.400
Please look forward
to Netflix Anime’s lineup in 2021!

01:19:31.150 --> 01:19:34.550
Now we move onto the next segment.

01:19:35.470 --> 01:19:38.660
-Now we play games.
-This is it.

01:19:38.720 --> 01:19:42.100
No skipping segments.

01:19:42.280 --> 01:19:46.280
Onto the game segment we go.

01:19:46.440 --> 01:19:51.930
We will ask out guests on stage today
to break into two teams.

01:19:51.960 --> 01:19:54.450
They will play some games for us.

01:19:54.570 --> 01:19:59.370
Please use your acting skills,
imagination, focus, observation,

01:19:59.390 --> 01:20:03.530
and skill to read the room
as voice actors to win the challenge!

01:20:03.730 --> 01:20:08.710
Shiraishi-san, Kaji-san and Tsuda-san
will be Team Mega.

01:20:08.810 --> 01:20:10.220
Team Mega!

01:20:10.250 --> 01:20:13.930
Kohno-san, Shimazaki-san,
and Kobayashi-san will be Team Rich.

01:20:14.160 --> 01:20:15.590
Team Rich!

01:20:15.770 --> 01:20:17.990
Team Mega and Team Rich.

01:20:18.040 --> 01:20:19.240
They have a god.

01:20:19.290 --> 01:20:23.510
No, no, no. You're all gods.

01:20:23.580 --> 01:20:27.270
It's Record of Ragnarok up here.

01:20:27.300 --> 01:20:31.340
So true.

01:20:31.540 --> 01:20:36.960
The team with more points
will win a prize at the end!

01:20:37.100 --> 01:20:39.460
Good luck to the contestants!

01:20:39.570 --> 01:20:43.050
Let's get started! What's the first game?

01:20:43.980 --> 01:20:46.820
Netflix Doubt!

01:20:48.710 --> 01:20:53.980
One team will be the presenter.
The other team will answer.

01:20:54.220 --> 01:20:57.580
The presenter will read stories off a card.

01:20:57.680 --> 01:21:01.130
However, only one card
has a complete story written on it.

01:21:01.280 --> 01:21:06.040
The other two members
only have rough plots.

01:21:06.120 --> 01:21:09.550
You must act and try to prevent
the answering team

01:21:09.570 --> 01:21:14.390
from guessing who is reading off the card
that has no complete story.

01:21:14.680 --> 01:21:18.590
The answering team must guess
which two drew the card with no story.

01:21:18.740 --> 01:21:25.330
In other words, guess which two
are making up their story on the spot.

01:21:25.530 --> 01:21:26.890
You have one shot to guess correctly.

01:21:27.850 --> 01:21:30.910
You guess right,
your team wins 10 points.

01:21:31.280 --> 01:21:35.190
The presenters will be tested on their acting skills.

01:21:35.310 --> 01:21:38.230
The answering team will be tested
on their observational skills.

01:21:38.360 --> 01:21:41.100
I hope you get the answers right.

01:21:41.350 --> 01:21:43.810
Let's get started.

01:21:43.870 --> 01:21:47.020
Team Mega goes first.

01:21:48.080 --> 01:21:54.650
There are three cards on the table.
One card has a complete story.

01:21:54.780 --> 01:21:57.090
The other two are rough plots.

01:21:57.220 --> 01:22:01.340
Shiraishi-san,
please go up and pick a card.

01:22:01.400 --> 01:22:03.140
-I'm nervous.
-Right?

01:22:03.190 --> 01:22:08.170
Please take a peek.
You can study her reaction as a clue.

01:22:08.350 --> 01:22:10.990
-It's already begun!
-That's right.

01:22:12.390 --> 01:22:16.500
-This is tough.
-Really rough.

01:22:16.750 --> 01:22:20.650
Take a peek but don't let them see.

01:22:22.730 --> 01:22:26.640
What does that mean?
Please return to your seat.

01:22:26.670 --> 01:22:29.550
-Was she relieved?
-Was she?

01:22:29.880 --> 01:22:31.080
Kaji-san.

01:22:31.260 --> 01:22:34.660
Will we find out who has the script?

01:22:35.170 --> 01:22:40.730
You'll find out later but not right now.

01:22:40.820 --> 01:22:45.180
Take a careful peek.

01:22:46.010 --> 01:22:50.750
What does it mean? His acting is superb.

01:22:50.810 --> 01:22:53.870
-The game is on!
-Tsuda-san.

01:22:57.130 --> 01:22:59.860
Step by step. He takes a a peek.

01:22:59.880 --> 01:23:02.360
He's so hot.

01:23:04.700 --> 01:23:06.590
-That face.
-Meaningful grin.

01:23:06.650 --> 01:23:08.900
-What does it mean?
-So sexy!

01:23:09.030 --> 01:23:14.900
When I say observe, I don't mean admire.
This is a game, remember?

01:23:15.580 --> 01:23:22.310
The cards are drawn.
Team Mega has 30 seconds to think.

01:23:22.340 --> 01:23:26.580
This is your chance to think of your story.

01:23:26.600 --> 01:23:32.610
We have an example for the viewers
so they know what to expect.

01:23:33.320 --> 01:23:36.920
As you can see, some elements
are included in all three cards.

01:23:36.990 --> 01:23:40.260
The opening line,
“My name is Seitaro Mukai!”

01:23:40.330 --> 01:23:43.070
You begin here.

01:23:43.210 --> 01:23:47.210
The character’s personality,
manner of speech,

01:23:47.370 --> 01:23:51.400
title, and closing line.

01:23:51.790 --> 01:23:56.500
One person has this
completely filled out card.

01:23:56.780 --> 01:24:00.620
The other two only have the outline.

01:24:01.730 --> 01:24:03.480
Just the themes.

01:24:04.370 --> 01:24:09.650
Team Rich keeps staring at Team Mega.

01:24:11.450 --> 01:24:16.550
You're just staring at each other.
Stop waving.

01:24:16.630 --> 01:24:17.770
Our eyes met. My heart skipped.

01:24:18.620 --> 01:24:20.130
Knock it off.

01:24:20.580 --> 01:24:26.480
Are you ready? Let's decide the order.

01:24:26.710 --> 01:24:29.400
Team Rich, close your eyes.

01:24:29.660 --> 01:24:33.290
Team Mega, decide your order.

01:24:35.890 --> 01:24:39.370
I'm OK with anything.

01:24:40.470 --> 01:24:42.090
Really?

01:24:42.250 --> 01:24:45.690
If you talk there's no point
in them closing their eyes.

01:24:45.770 --> 01:24:49.770
You've got to gesture.

01:24:49.870 --> 01:24:51.060
You can choose.

01:24:57.130 --> 01:25:02.300
Team Rich, please open your eyes.

01:25:02.360 --> 01:25:07.630
Will the presenter please stand?

01:25:07.940 --> 01:25:11.540
Netflix Doubt Start!

01:25:13.800 --> 01:25:16.570
I'm Seitaro Mukai.

01:25:16.730 --> 01:25:18.000
Character setting.

01:25:18.440 --> 01:25:20.190
Girlfriendless for 35 years.

01:25:20.300 --> 01:25:26.740
Currently jobless. I run into a childhood
friend who grew up to be beautiful.

01:25:27.800 --> 01:25:29.980
Monologue.

01:25:30.110 --> 01:25:33.170
Let's be close like we used to be?

01:25:33.450 --> 01:25:35.500
Wha-!? It says, "wha-!?"

01:25:36.270 --> 01:25:37.970
The title is

01:25:38.530 --> 01:25:42.870
Is a Jobless 35-Year-Old Allowed
 to Hang Out With a Hot Girl?

01:25:44.510 --> 01:25:45.530
What a title.

01:25:45.790 --> 01:25:46.940
The line I have to read.

01:25:47.260 --> 01:25:51.510
"Call me Sei-chan like you used to."

01:25:53.170 --> 01:25:56.880
Thank you. Very nice.

01:25:57.070 --> 01:26:00.700
Can we say the genre? It's romantic comedy.

01:26:01.980 --> 01:26:09.400
May we have the second presenter?

01:26:09.950 --> 01:26:12.080
Please begin!

01:26:14.080 --> 01:26:16.430
My name is Seitaro Mukai!

01:26:17.950 --> 01:26:20.650
I'm starting high school today.

01:26:23.290 --> 01:26:28.850
They thought I was groping a girl
on the bus on the way to school.

01:26:28.870 --> 01:26:31.250
What?

01:26:33.110 --> 01:26:35.880
What a rough start to the first day of school.

01:26:36.250 --> 01:26:43.730
When I arrive at the classroom
I spot the girl that I groped in the bus!

01:26:43.760 --> 01:26:48.600
-You groped her?
-Who accused me, that is.

01:26:48.820 --> 01:26:51.370
Our love story begins.

01:26:51.620 --> 01:26:55.950
Of course we had no idea back then.

01:26:55.990 --> 01:26:57.360
I see.

01:26:57.680 --> 01:26:59.080
Title.

01:26:59.590 --> 01:27:03.880
-Seitaro Mukai! A Beast In Love
-Beast?

01:27:04.190 --> 01:27:07.380
-Beast?
-The line.

01:27:08.280 --> 01:27:12.100
"I know you got the hots for me! Fess up!"

01:27:12.320 --> 01:27:15.480
Nice. Thank you!

01:27:15.590 --> 01:27:20.340
What a hot beast!

01:27:20.670 --> 01:27:24.170
-It must be like Beauty and the Beast.
-I see.

01:27:24.890 --> 01:27:30.250
Tsuda-san, if you will.

01:27:33.090 --> 01:27:35.160
I'm Seitaro Mukai.

01:27:37.670 --> 01:27:40.690
I'm 35, from Cuba,
and I'm starting high school.

01:27:40.800 --> 01:27:43.380
That's a lot to digest.

01:27:45.450 --> 01:27:48.390
My hand touched another on the bus.

01:27:48.620 --> 01:27:49.990
He did it.

01:27:50.320 --> 01:27:53.650
But it was the back side of my hand.

01:27:53.840 --> 01:27:56.310
Still not OK.

01:27:56.410 --> 01:27:59.140
It was an accident. I'm sorry.

01:27:59.650 --> 01:28:02.890
But I'm Cubano.

01:28:03.020 --> 01:28:07.450
-So what?
-I'm a man of passion.

01:28:08.580 --> 01:28:10.690
Title.

01:28:12.190 --> 01:28:13.730
Man From Cuba.

01:28:13.800 --> 01:28:15.980
So straightforward.

01:28:18.140 --> 01:28:19.420
The line.

01:28:20.380 --> 01:28:23.120
-"Just a little bit."
-Huh?

01:28:24.840 --> 01:28:26.910
What a title.

01:28:27.270 --> 01:28:29.790
When does he say the line?

01:28:30.390 --> 01:28:35.260
-We really captured the characters well.
-Are you sure?

01:28:35.540 --> 01:28:37.920
Two out of three were groping people!

01:28:39.460 --> 01:28:41.910
It might be what the script said.

01:28:42.150 --> 01:28:45.960
What did you think, Team Rich?

01:28:46.050 --> 01:28:50.000
Do you want to discuss?

01:28:51.530 --> 01:28:56.390
Tsuda-san's line at the end

01:28:56.470 --> 01:29:00.210
was suddenly on the receiving end.

01:29:00.230 --> 01:29:04.440
That switch had to have come
from Tsuda-san himself.

01:29:05.710 --> 01:29:11.820
He was explaining his innocence,
then suddenly he is on the receiving end.

01:29:11.880 --> 01:29:13.790
Out of the blue.

01:29:13.910 --> 01:29:17.870
That has to be Tsuda-san.

01:29:17.940 --> 01:29:20.400
Great analysis.

01:29:20.660 --> 01:29:23.620
So you choose Tsuda-san?

01:29:23.870 --> 01:29:27.420
-He had a rough plot?
-Yes.

01:29:27.460 --> 01:29:30.190
Who else?

01:29:30.240 --> 01:29:37.730
Kaji-san wouldn't get the role of the beast
with such a pretty voice.

01:29:38.220 --> 01:29:41.260
Sudden criticism?

01:29:43.380 --> 01:29:47.930
My feelings are hurt.
I want to be the beast too.

01:29:49.200 --> 01:29:51.620
Netflix, please cast me as the beast.

01:29:51.680 --> 01:29:52.970
He can play the beast too.

01:29:53.040 --> 01:29:57.010
A beast may have a pretty voice.

01:29:57.050 --> 01:30:06.010
But this is Kaji-san.
He can do a beast voice if he wants to.

01:30:06.250 --> 01:30:08.160
I see.

01:30:08.600 --> 01:30:14.380
If he has the script,
he will prepare for it.

01:30:14.690 --> 01:30:21.090
That's why I think
his natural hotness came through.

01:30:21.220 --> 01:30:23.480
He is naturally too hot.

01:30:24.240 --> 01:30:25.960
His hotness overwrote the beast?

01:30:27.280 --> 01:30:33.090
Then can we agree on the answer?

01:30:33.190 --> 01:30:39.140
That means Shiraishi-san is the culprit!

01:30:39.420 --> 01:30:40.750
Culprit?

01:30:40.770 --> 01:30:43.660
That's not the game.

01:30:43.730 --> 01:30:48.000
Shiraishi-san is the honest one.
The other two are liars.

01:30:48.030 --> 01:30:54.410
That's right. She has the script.

01:30:54.510 --> 01:30:58.040
You think Kaji-san and Tsuda-san are lying?

01:30:58.200 --> 01:30:59.540
-Yes!
-OK.

01:30:59.640 --> 01:31:11.740
On my signal, will the people without the script
please show your cards to the camera?

01:31:12.050 --> 01:31:17.220
On the count of two. One, two!

01:31:20.850 --> 01:31:24.460
There you have it! Team Rich got it wrong!

01:31:24.610 --> 01:31:28.030
Team Mega deceived them!

01:31:28.140 --> 01:31:30.810
Incredible!

01:31:30.900 --> 01:31:38.640
I have a feeling this was all a part of their plan.

01:31:39.090 --> 01:31:41.840
I had the script.

01:31:42.680 --> 01:31:45.620
-I'm so sorry.
-It's OK.

01:31:45.800 --> 01:31:47.280
We fooled you.

01:31:47.440 --> 01:31:55.580
-She did a great job.
-Read so smoothly.

01:31:55.650 --> 01:31:58.510
It was my plan.

01:31:58.610 --> 01:32:04.420
I was wondering what the others would do.

01:32:04.450 --> 01:32:09.420
She volunteered to go first.

01:32:09.460 --> 01:32:17.030
I followed her lead and pretended
to stumble my lines.

01:32:18.110 --> 01:32:24.010
Then Tsuda-san went along perfectly for us.

01:32:24.310 --> 01:32:29.570
He made the perfect blend for us.

01:32:29.670 --> 01:32:34.870
It's Team Rich's turn.

01:32:34.940 --> 01:32:37.460
Please come and get your card.

01:32:37.590 --> 01:32:38.890
OK!

01:32:38.940 --> 01:32:41.180
They're watching your reaction!

01:32:41.430 --> 01:32:44.950
This is important!

01:32:47.160 --> 01:32:49.090
There you go!

01:32:49.450 --> 01:32:51.320
What was that?

01:32:51.710 --> 01:32:53.620
Shimasaki-san.

01:32:54.190 --> 01:32:56.750
This is a big clue.

01:32:56.970 --> 01:32:59.200
Looking back, you can tell.

01:32:59.350 --> 01:33:02.390
He takes a peek.

01:33:02.420 --> 01:33:04.260
What is this?

01:33:04.440 --> 01:33:05.950
The universe has spoken.

01:33:06.040 --> 01:33:09.970
-You have spoken.
-Something is fishy.

01:33:10.020 --> 01:33:12.480
Kobayashi-san.

01:33:15.230 --> 01:33:18.350
He's already acting.

01:33:18.610 --> 01:33:23.000
There's only one card. Just take it!

01:33:23.330 --> 01:33:26.850
What could that expression mean?

01:33:26.890 --> 01:33:29.630
He looks like he can do housework!

01:33:29.780 --> 01:33:31.620
That's got nothing to do with this.

01:33:31.900 --> 01:33:34.000
-But he can't cook rice!
-Knock it off.

01:33:34.080 --> 01:33:36.000
You can tell all that?

01:33:36.030 --> 01:33:39.330
You have 30 seconds to think.

01:33:39.520 --> 01:33:44.190
Team Mega, you did so well.

01:33:44.220 --> 01:33:48.340
I didn't expect it to work so well.

01:33:48.480 --> 01:33:52.120
What was that about Cuba?

01:33:52.150 --> 01:33:53.110
It just popped into my mind.

01:33:53.160 --> 01:33:57.040
-But you ran with it to the end.
-Yeah.

01:33:57.200 --> 01:34:01.110
It even ended up in the title.

01:34:01.170 --> 01:34:02.200
Great job.

01:34:02.220 --> 01:34:05.660
We had a turn at presenting
so we have an advantage.

01:34:05.770 --> 01:34:09.450
We can guess where
the other team might be lying.

01:34:09.510 --> 01:34:10.790
Very true.

01:34:10.930 --> 01:34:14.160
Team Rich must take that into account.

01:34:14.240 --> 01:34:17.620
Team Mega, please close your eyes.

01:34:17.720 --> 01:34:20.460
Team Rich, how will you present?

01:34:26.910 --> 01:34:30.710
They are deciding. Are you ready?

01:34:32.300 --> 01:34:37.100
OK. Please open your eyes.

01:34:37.330 --> 01:34:44.420
Team Rich Netflix Doubt, start!

01:34:44.750 --> 01:34:46.100
-Who is first?
-Me!

01:34:46.150 --> 01:34:47.700
-Kohno-san?
-Yes!

01:34:48.430 --> 01:34:49.490
Please start!

01:34:53.670 --> 01:34:57.350
My name is Seitaro Mukai!

01:34:57.840 --> 01:34:59.760
-I'm five!
-Just a kid!

01:35:02.160 --> 01:35:07.740
I often get bullied,
but one day I met Blank-chan!

01:35:08.800 --> 01:35:10.820
-I mean, Marika-chan!
-Marika-chan?

01:35:12.490 --> 01:35:18.550
I decided to be a hero
to protect Marika-chan!

01:35:19.540 --> 01:35:21.090
A Tiny Hero.

01:35:22.680 --> 01:35:25.540
Never Fear! I will protect you, Marika-chan!

01:35:26.790 --> 01:35:29.480
Thank you!

01:35:29.780 --> 01:35:33.050
-They do a hero series.
-All of them?

01:35:33.100 --> 01:35:35.960
- I see.
-Her title is "A Tiny Hero"?

01:35:36.040 --> 01:35:37.850
-Is it?
-Yes.

01:35:38.420 --> 01:35:42.880
Who is second?

01:35:44.850 --> 01:35:48.880
Kobayashi-san? Let's begin!

01:35:51.400 --> 01:35:54.070
My name is Seitaro Mukai!

01:35:56.880 --> 01:36:01.050
I am a super hero that protects this town.

01:36:02.010 --> 01:36:05.050
However, no one knows this.

01:36:06.860 --> 01:36:09.440
I wear...

01:36:11.070 --> 01:36:12.120
Let's see...

01:36:12.880 --> 01:36:15.030
-Tights.
-What?

01:36:15.140 --> 01:36:19.770
I clad myself in full-body tights

01:36:19.800 --> 01:36:25.280
and patrol the town!

01:36:25.450 --> 01:36:26.690
You'll get arrested.

01:36:28.030 --> 01:36:30.480
I fight an evil entity.

01:36:32.530 --> 01:36:38.030
They send one enemy after the other
for me to take down!

01:36:41.310 --> 01:36:42.120
Special Attack

01:36:43.300 --> 01:36:44.300
Mukai katta!

01:36:44.500 --> 01:36:45.680
What's that?

01:36:48.420 --> 01:36:50.400
I have protected the peace once again!

01:36:51.350 --> 01:36:53.220
The title.

01:36:56.570 --> 01:36:57.530
Superhuman

01:36:59.940 --> 01:37:01.880
Superhuman Squadron Mukai

01:37:02.170 --> 01:37:03.110
Mukai Mask Man

01:37:03.270 --> 01:37:06.010
Are you alone or are you a squadron?

01:37:06.040 --> 01:37:11.660
Never Fear! No matter what, I will protect you!

01:37:12.360 --> 01:37:16.790
Thank you. Nice wrap up.

01:37:17.370 --> 01:37:19.960
We had Mukai Kamen Man.

01:37:20.300 --> 01:37:22.400
Shimazaki-san, are you ready?

01:37:22.530 --> 01:37:26.260
Please read your story.

01:37:27.960 --> 01:37:30.640
My name is Seitaro Mukai.

01:37:31.480 --> 01:37:34.420
I go to Seija Private High School.

01:37:35.750 --> 01:37:38.880
However, it is only a diguise.

01:37:39.760 --> 01:37:44.730
I am a dark hero
with memories of my past life.

01:37:45.060 --> 01:37:47.800
-I am Justice Blade.
-Justice Blade?

01:37:48.750 --> 01:37:51.920
I serve justice with the power of darkness.

01:37:52.240 --> 01:37:56.200
The era of serving justice
to evil is over.

01:37:56.700 --> 01:37:59.230
Evil judges evil!

01:37:59.510 --> 01:38:04.130
It is I, Justice Blade,
who will judge evil!

01:38:04.920 --> 01:38:10.070
Witness the story of Justice Blade's
battles in darkness!

01:38:11.910 --> 01:38:14.060
Dark hero, Justice Blade.

01:38:14.650 --> 01:38:17.000
Say the line with me!

01:38:17.660 --> 01:38:20.000
Three, two, one!

01:38:21.190 --> 01:38:24.150
"Dark blade cutting through the night!"

01:38:24.340 --> 01:38:25.810
What?

01:38:26.030 --> 01:38:28.480
Thank you!

01:38:29.670 --> 01:38:34.080
There you go. Three hero plots.

01:38:34.340 --> 01:38:40.310
Please decide who had the script.

01:38:40.400 --> 01:38:45.240
Shimazaki-san wasn't looking at the card.

01:38:45.370 --> 01:38:48.900
I already memorized it.

01:38:49.000 --> 01:38:51.150
You did?

01:38:51.180 --> 01:38:54.030
I did add my own twist to it.

01:38:54.080 --> 01:38:55.760
He's lying.

01:38:56.130 --> 01:38:58.930
Do you think so?

01:38:59.280 --> 01:39:03.260
-Who else?
-I think Kohno-san.

01:39:06.130 --> 01:39:09.950
Kobayashi-kun was reading badly on purpose.

01:39:10.050 --> 01:39:14.630
But it might be a decoy.

01:39:14.670 --> 01:39:22.740
Kohno-san said "Blank-chan,"
then Marika-chan.

01:39:23.540 --> 01:39:29.780
Did she read the script wrong and fix it?

01:39:30.130 --> 01:39:33.970
Or was that all acting too?

01:39:34.630 --> 01:39:38.030
Who will Team Mega choose?

01:39:38.150 --> 01:39:40.170
Shiraishi-san will choose.

01:39:40.320 --> 01:39:45.550
Well Uh... Shimazaki-san....

01:39:45.580 --> 01:39:47.860
And Kohno-san.

01:39:47.890 --> 01:39:49.130
I see.

01:39:49.250 --> 01:39:55.370
Did Team Mega get it right?

01:39:55.390 --> 01:40:04.110
Please show your cards on my cue. One, two!

01:40:05.250 --> 01:40:06.660
You fell for it!

01:40:06.690 --> 01:40:10.230
Team Mega got it right!

01:40:10.300 --> 01:40:14.440
Incredible!

01:40:14.810 --> 01:40:20.660
You got it right. Team Rich seems so sad.

01:40:20.720 --> 01:40:26.060
I was so nervous I drank the whole bottle.

01:40:26.370 --> 01:40:31.200
-They saw through me!
-You didn't read the card!

01:40:31.940 --> 01:40:35.130
You couldn't have memorized it.

01:40:36.570 --> 01:40:42.830
Team Mega earned ten points.
Team Rich earned zero points.

01:40:42.940 --> 01:40:44.850
That’s all for “Netflix Doubt”!

01:40:44.990 --> 01:40:47.820
Let’s move on to the next game.

01:40:47.850 --> 01:40:52.340
The next game is “Netflix Search”!

01:40:52.370 --> 01:40:56.720
This is the last game.

01:40:56.920 --> 01:41:01.860
I will read out keywords associated
with a particular anime title.

01:41:01.960 --> 01:41:05.860
You must try and guess it.

01:41:06.030 --> 01:41:10.190
New keywords will be added
as time progresses.

01:41:10.330 --> 01:41:12.220
Press the button as soon
as you know what title it is.

01:41:12.600 --> 01:41:16.530
When your lamp lights up,
use the tablet to search for the title.

01:41:16.590 --> 01:41:21.020
Then, show it on your screen to answer.

01:41:21.060 --> 01:41:24.410
Please press the button after
you have searched the title.

01:41:24.540 --> 01:41:27.610
So the titles are streaming on Netflix?

01:41:27.960 --> 01:41:31.140
Of course.

01:41:31.500 --> 01:41:36.220
I watch Netflix a lot.
I was watching yesterday too.

01:41:36.250 --> 01:41:39.360
Good.

01:41:39.470 --> 01:41:42.850
You might have an advantage.

01:41:43.060 --> 01:41:49.100
If you answer incorrectly, the opposing team
will be given the right to answer.

01:41:49.210 --> 01:41:52.940
Please keep that in mind.

01:41:53.010 --> 01:41:56.140
Your imagination
and inspiration will be tested.

01:41:56.160 --> 01:41:58.790
Each correct answer will earn you five points.

01:41:58.990 --> 01:42:03.600
Let's go. Are you ready?

01:42:03.630 --> 01:42:08.360
“Netflix Search,” start!

01:42:09.070 --> 01:42:15.440
You will get a clue every 10 seconds.

01:42:15.730 --> 01:42:18.680
Finger.

01:42:18.770 --> 01:42:22.060
Buzz in if you know.

01:42:22.340 --> 01:42:25.360
Shimazaki-san!

01:42:25.470 --> 01:42:27.560
I watch this.

01:42:27.690 --> 01:42:31.000
Your answer please!

01:42:32.290 --> 01:42:33.570
Itaewon Class!

01:42:34.480 --> 01:42:35.490
No?

01:42:35.890 --> 01:42:36.860
Nope.

01:42:37.010 --> 01:42:39.290
But this finger!

01:42:40.160 --> 01:42:43.860
So much for watching Netflix all the time.

01:42:45.310 --> 01:42:50.470
Of course not.
We're talking about anime.

01:42:51.120 --> 01:42:55.040
Team Mega can answer now.

01:42:55.070 --> 01:42:57.710
-No new clues?
-No.

01:42:57.740 --> 01:43:01.310
Please answer as is.

01:43:02.340 --> 01:43:04.870
We can move on too.

01:43:04.960 --> 01:43:09.530
Shiraishi-san?

01:43:09.590 --> 01:43:10.840
This anime!

01:43:11.020 --> 01:43:13.370
The Disastrous Life of Saiki K.

01:43:13.560 --> 01:43:17.810
Wrong.

01:43:17.840 --> 01:43:22.920
It's not about fingers being in the banner.

01:43:23.860 --> 01:43:26.360
It's a free for all.

01:43:26.510 --> 01:43:29.750
Let's see more clues.

01:43:29.890 --> 01:43:34.510
Negative emotions. Finger.

01:43:34.590 --> 01:43:39.470
Kobayashi-san. Please answer.

01:43:39.900 --> 01:43:41.030
Non Non Biyori.

01:43:42.230 --> 01:43:43.410
Not possible.

01:43:44.470 --> 01:43:46.410
No negative emotions there.

01:43:46.610 --> 01:43:50.370
All happiness. It's a recovery potion.

01:43:50.400 --> 01:43:53.320
Mega Team, over to you.

01:43:53.690 --> 01:43:58.750
If you don't answer, it's a free for all.

01:43:59.170 --> 01:44:01.340
Can you answer?

01:44:03.950 --> 01:44:09.030
Kaji-san? Your answer?

01:44:09.060 --> 01:44:13.060
-I have to search?
-Yes.

01:44:14.230 --> 01:44:17.330
-Is it there?
-No?

01:44:19.730 --> 01:44:22.860
Is he timidly playing the piano?

01:44:23.170 --> 01:44:28.410
It's not the one I thought.

01:44:28.460 --> 01:44:30.850
You're out of time!

01:44:31.270 --> 01:44:35.180
You can all answer.

01:44:35.400 --> 01:44:38.630
We have a new clue.

01:44:39.850 --> 01:44:43.240
High school.

01:44:43.380 --> 01:44:44.430
Do you have the screen?

01:44:44.510 --> 01:44:47.980
I got inspired by Non Non Biyori.

01:44:48.000 --> 01:44:49.920
Really?

01:44:50.020 --> 01:44:52.710
Your answer please.

01:44:53.290 --> 01:44:54.330
Jujutsu Kaisen!

01:44:54.750 --> 01:44:56.290
That's right!

01:44:57.210 --> 01:45:01.280
How is that connected to Non Non Biyori?

01:45:01.370 --> 01:45:04.480
It's team play.

01:45:04.510 --> 01:45:06.990
Wonderful.

01:45:07.040 --> 01:45:10.790
Please search the title
then press the button to answer.

01:45:11.070 --> 01:45:16.620
The next question is this.

01:45:17.160 --> 01:45:20.420
Humanity.

01:45:21.510 --> 01:45:24.230
Humanity.

01:45:24.370 --> 01:45:29.450
It could be anything.
It could be Non Non Biyori.

01:45:29.480 --> 01:45:31.080
Could be.

01:45:31.300 --> 01:45:36.920
What's the next clue?

01:45:37.600 --> 01:45:38.540
Here it comes.

01:45:38.570 --> 01:45:40.960
Heart.

01:45:43.880 --> 01:45:45.340
Oh no.

01:45:45.370 --> 01:45:49.950
Do you have the screen ready?
Please answer.

01:45:50.480 --> 01:45:51.740
Attack on Titan!

01:45:52.560 --> 01:45:54.220
Yes!

01:45:54.280 --> 01:45:55.410
Dedicate your heart!

01:45:55.470 --> 01:45:57.070
Thank you!

01:45:57.640 --> 01:46:02.310
I already thought of it at "humanity,"
but it could have been Non Non Biyori.

01:46:02.340 --> 01:46:03.980
Could be.

01:46:04.060 --> 01:46:06.220
They have hearts too.

01:46:06.280 --> 01:46:08.500
But I took a chance.

01:46:08.520 --> 01:46:12.610
You won five points.

01:46:13.200 --> 01:46:16.970
Next question.

01:46:17.610 --> 01:46:24.140
Los Angeles.

01:46:24.360 --> 01:46:28.690
What could it be?

01:46:29.160 --> 01:46:32.940
Not Non Non Biyori.

01:46:33.120 --> 01:46:36.870
Singapore.
Los Angeles. Singapore.

01:46:36.910 --> 01:46:38.680
International.

01:46:38.720 --> 01:46:45.410
Please get the title ready
then press your button.

01:46:45.470 --> 01:46:48.980
London.

01:46:51.610 --> 01:46:56.410
Maybe they visit these places.

01:46:57.040 --> 01:46:59.980
Shanghai.

01:47:00.820 --> 01:47:02.220
Shanghai?

01:47:03.460 --> 01:47:07.820
Kobayashi-san, your answer please!

01:47:08.190 --> 01:47:09.470
Great Pretender!

01:47:11.600 --> 01:47:13.350
Wonderful.

01:47:13.600 --> 01:47:18.520
The four locations rang a bell?

01:47:18.660 --> 01:47:24.000
Five points! Well done!
Keep it up!

01:47:24.200 --> 01:47:26.000
Next question.

01:47:28.230 --> 01:47:29.430
Hakone.

01:47:31.580 --> 01:47:38.210
Another location.
What is located in Hakone?

01:47:38.690 --> 01:47:42.020
14 years old.

01:47:43.680 --> 01:47:47.400
Hakone. 14 years old.

01:47:47.560 --> 01:47:50.720
-Tsuda-san.
-Evangelion.

01:47:50.880 --> 01:47:51.750
Tsuda-san.

01:47:54.290 --> 01:47:57.190
-Neon Genesis Evangelion.
-Correct!

01:47:57.300 --> 01:47:59.810
So fast!

01:48:00.860 --> 01:48:03.730
-That was easy.
-Yes.

01:48:03.820 --> 01:48:06.290
You were so fast.

01:48:07.010 --> 01:48:08.670
Five points!

01:48:08.850 --> 01:48:11.740
What a great battle!

01:48:12.090 --> 01:48:14.340
Next question!

01:48:16.020 --> 01:48:18.220
The keyword is...

01:48:18.560 --> 01:48:20.630
Ship.

01:48:21.180 --> 01:48:25.530
Does it ring a bell?

01:48:26.990 --> 01:48:29.660
Does Non Non Biyori visit the sea?

01:48:29.730 --> 01:48:31.010
No.

01:48:31.100 --> 01:48:32.640
Sword.

01:48:33.560 --> 01:48:37.220
That was close!

01:48:37.450 --> 01:48:40.510
Shimazaki-san, please answer!

01:48:41.280 --> 01:48:42.210
One Piece!

01:48:43.700 --> 01:48:44.820
Correct!

01:48:46.430 --> 01:48:47.650
Yes!

01:48:48.380 --> 01:48:51.640
I'm in it! I have to get it right!

01:48:52.230 --> 01:48:53.940
Shiraishi-san had it too.

01:48:54.000 --> 01:48:57.600
Yes. I had the screen open.

01:48:57.790 --> 01:49:02.590
It was so close.
This is like a real quiz show.

01:49:02.800 --> 01:49:06.080
On to the next question!

01:49:07.010 --> 01:49:08.020
Here it comes.

01:49:08.130 --> 01:49:09.970
Vampire.

01:49:11.350 --> 01:49:15.240
Vampire. What could it be?

01:49:15.310 --> 01:49:18.980
There are many vampire anime.

01:49:20.500 --> 01:49:21.420
What's next?

01:49:21.670 --> 01:49:24.800
Pillar.

01:49:25.290 --> 01:49:28.530
Yes, Tsuda-san?

01:49:29.820 --> 01:49:30.950
Demon Slayer!

01:49:32.580 --> 01:49:33.440
That's not it!

01:49:34.550 --> 01:49:38.230
I know you thought that at "pillar."

01:49:38.640 --> 01:49:44.000
You fell right for the trap. Thank you.

01:49:44.630 --> 01:49:47.500
This is exactly what we planned for.

01:49:47.730 --> 01:49:52.650
You got it wrong so Team Rich
has the right to answer.

01:49:52.960 --> 01:49:55.370
Would someone like to answer?

01:49:55.880 --> 01:49:58.410
Vampire and pillar?

01:49:58.680 --> 01:49:59.960
Not Non Non Biyori.

01:50:00.080 --> 01:50:04.580
They don't have vampires.

01:50:06.070 --> 01:50:09.000
Your answer please!

01:50:09.290 --> 01:50:10.240
Devil's Line!

01:50:11.610 --> 01:50:17.390
Anyone can answer. New clue please!

01:50:17.870 --> 01:50:19.820
Bow and arrow.

01:50:19.970 --> 01:50:24.220
Kobayashi-san.

01:50:24.550 --> 01:50:26.400
Jojo's Bizarre Story.

01:50:27.250 --> 01:50:28.630
Yes!

01:50:29.330 --> 01:50:30.070
Yes!

01:50:30.380 --> 01:50:33.250
Jojo's Bizarre Adventure. Close enough!

01:50:33.330 --> 01:50:37.900
Wonderful.

01:50:37.930 --> 01:50:41.700
The final question!

01:50:42.070 --> 01:50:45.600
The first clue.

01:50:47.080 --> 01:50:50.870
- God.
-Tsuda-san?

01:50:50.920 --> 01:50:54.230
-No way.
-Me?

01:50:54.260 --> 01:51:00.350
A show about him?

01:51:00.370 --> 01:51:03.640
Devil.

01:51:03.670 --> 01:51:09.070
He's also a devil.
God. Devil.

01:51:09.180 --> 01:51:13.060
It can't be Tsuda-san.

01:51:13.080 --> 01:51:15.830
Could be it?

01:51:15.860 --> 01:51:20.050
Crybaby.

01:51:21.580 --> 01:51:26.750
-You could be more confused.
-True.

01:51:27.080 --> 01:51:31.560
That's the third clue.

01:51:31.590 --> 01:51:32.750
Satan.

01:51:33.750 --> 01:51:37.020
Crybaby. Satan.

01:51:37.520 --> 01:51:39.310
Is it too hard?

01:51:39.330 --> 01:51:44.460
Kobayashi-san, please answer.

01:51:45.060 --> 01:51:47.040
-Non Non Biyori.
-No!

01:51:48.100 --> 01:51:51.380
Apologize!

01:51:52.160 --> 01:51:54.950
They never had Satan!

01:51:55.810 --> 01:52:00.340
Mega Team, any takers?

01:52:01.080 --> 01:52:05.000
You can take a stab.

01:52:06.980 --> 01:52:11.290
You might run out of time.

01:52:12.890 --> 01:52:15.390
Crybaby?

01:52:16.050 --> 01:52:23.620
We're out of time. New clues please.

01:52:24.350 --> 01:52:27.910
Rap.

01:52:33.590 --> 01:52:37.590
Dancing won't help.

01:52:39.080 --> 01:52:42.830
Director Masaaki Yuasa

01:52:49.490 --> 01:52:52.420
How about now?

01:52:53.480 --> 01:53:00.180
Shimazaki-san! Please answer.

01:53:00.250 --> 01:53:01.270
Devilman.

01:53:02.810 --> 01:53:06.650
Yes, that's right!

01:53:06.670 --> 01:53:10.640
I thought so.

01:53:10.690 --> 01:53:15.110
The protagonist is a crybaby.

01:53:15.200 --> 01:53:18.270
That's all with the games.

01:53:18.310 --> 01:53:25.980
Let's look at the points.

01:53:26.020 --> 01:53:31.790
Team Mega 10 points. Team Rich 25 points.

01:53:31.860 --> 01:53:33.990
Congrats Team Rich!

01:53:36.620 --> 01:53:43.930
We have the final results.

01:53:44.490 --> 01:53:47.210
Team Mega 20 points.

01:53:47.650 --> 01:53:50.920
Team Rich 25 points.

01:53:51.130 --> 01:53:55.230
Team Rich is the winner!

01:53:55.690 --> 01:53:57.410
Congratulations!

01:53:57.590 --> 01:53:59.480
Thanks to Non Non Biyori!

01:53:59.510 --> 01:54:03.270
I should have taken away points for that!

01:54:03.300 --> 01:54:05.850
Congratulations.

01:54:06.230 --> 01:54:11.090
The winning team will be presented
with a “Netflix Mega-Rich Happy Bag,”

01:54:11.120 --> 01:54:16.400
which is mega-rich
with Netflix original merch!

01:54:16.640 --> 01:54:24.070
It's packed! Please look forward to it.

01:54:24.330 --> 01:54:26.760
Congratulations!

01:54:28.460 --> 01:54:31.360
I hope you enjoyed the game segment!

01:54:31.460 --> 01:54:39.220
It's already time for the ending.
How time flies.

01:54:39.240 --> 01:54:43.880
Could we have a word from our guests
for our viewers?

01:54:44.020 --> 01:54:45.950
Shiraishi-san?

01:54:45.980 --> 01:54:49.650
Thank you for watching today.

01:54:49.720 --> 01:54:54.700
Thank you for letting me introduce
High-Rise Invasion today.

01:54:54.730 --> 01:55:00.680
I am even more excited
about Netflix Anime now.

01:55:00.700 --> 01:55:07.350
What's great about Netflix
is that you can binge watch.

01:55:07.460 --> 01:55:11.010
Please binge watch
High-Rise Invasion many times.

01:55:11.100 --> 01:55:15.110
-Thanks for today.
-Thank you!

01:55:15.730 --> 01:55:17.650
Kaji-san?

01:55:17.810 --> 01:55:20.250
Thank you for watching.

01:55:20.530 --> 01:55:25.290
B: the Beginning is in its second season.

01:55:25.390 --> 01:55:29.570
If you watch you'll get hooked.

01:55:29.760 --> 01:55:36.310
Today I discovered shows
I'd like to start watching.

01:55:36.350 --> 01:55:41.070
Maybe the viewers did too.

01:55:41.210 --> 01:55:48.380
I hope you'll deepen
your love for anime too.

01:55:48.510 --> 01:55:52.120
Please keep watching Netflix Anime.

01:55:52.210 --> 01:55:54.340
Thank you.

01:55:54.370 --> 01:55:56.280
Tsuda-san?

01:55:56.420 --> 01:56:02.120
I'm Tsuda, a.k.a. god.
Thank you.

01:56:02.240 --> 01:56:08.350
The Way of the Househusband
will start streaming really soon.

01:56:08.450 --> 01:56:15.780
It'll start April 8th,
so please look forward to it.

01:56:15.820 --> 01:56:21.520
It has amazing characters and story.

01:56:21.590 --> 01:56:27.720
It's something you can kick back and enjoy.

01:56:27.770 --> 01:56:34.420
Like they said,
I got to know new shows tonight.

01:56:34.740 --> 01:56:39.470
I'm going to binge watch too.

01:56:39.500 --> 01:56:48.560
I think that's what is amazing about Netflix Anime.

01:56:48.620 --> 01:56:53.360
Please invite me back
when you have another show like this.

01:56:53.450 --> 01:56:54.680
Thank you.

01:56:55.717 --> 01:56:57.050
Next, Kohno-san.

01:56:58.250 --> 01:57:01.250
I'm Mariko Kohno from Eden!

01:57:01.250 --> 01:57:07.050
It's an original series,
so there's not much info yet...

01:57:07.050 --> 01:57:13.210
but it's a drama with humans against robots.

01:57:13.210 --> 01:57:18.480
If robots had human emotions,
would they try to eliminate humans?

01:57:18.480 --> 01:57:24.310
If humans were in that world, what would happen to robots?

01:57:24.310 --> 01:57:29.710
It's a thought-provoking series!
Please do check it out!

01:57:29.710 --> 01:57:35.110
It was fun to spend time with these "godly" voice actors! Thanks!

01:57:36.910 --> 01:57:38.550
Shimazaki-san, please.

01:57:38.550 --> 01:57:40.950
You're a voice acting god too!

01:57:44.410 --> 01:57:52.680
It was so fun!
And I'm excited to see everyone's shows!

01:57:52.680 --> 01:58:00.180
Netflix Anime titles span every genre,
and they're high-quality and interesting.

01:58:00.180 --> 01:58:11.880
I want to recommend them to everyone!

01:58:11.880 --> 01:58:20.050
As for BAKI, Baki Hanma is coming,
and every previous season is available now.

01:58:20.050 --> 01:58:28.850
You could watch them all from beginning to end!

01:58:28.850 --> 01:58:33.080
They're all great! Thanks!

01:58:34.210 --> 01:58:35.810
Kobayashi-san!

01:58:35.810 --> 01:58:43.510
Thanks for watching, everyone!
It was my first time promoting Spriggan at an event.

01:58:43.510 --> 01:58:50.380
I hope I was able to communicate its charms a little.

01:58:50.380 --> 01:58:57.510
As everyone said, there's tons of great anime on Netflix.

01:58:57.510 --> 01:59:08.080
And you can watch anytime.
Before bed, in the bath, while on the train...

01:59:08.080 --> 01:59:14.110
And sorry to all the Non Non Biyori fans!

01:59:14.110 --> 01:59:16.310
-Sorry!
-I do love it!

01:59:16.310 --> 01:59:25.210
There'll be lots more about Spriggan soon.
Please look forward to it!

01:59:27.780 --> 01:59:31.580
High-Rise Invasion and B: The Beginning are streaming now.

01:59:31.580 --> 01:59:34.610
The Way of the Househusband is coming April 8.

01:59:34.610 --> 01:59:37.550
Eden is coming May 27.

01:59:37.550 --> 01:59:41.080
Baki Hanma and Spriggan are coming in 2021.

01:59:41.080 --> 01:59:46.280
Every show will premiere worldwide at the same time!

01:59:46.280 --> 01:59:51.750
Thank you for watching! Goodbye!

